    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (73.81) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (73.72) anchor the LawDog lineup as our premier daily plays. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to a soft matchup against Jose Quintana, and his placement in the #3 hole provides the run-production upside we need to stay competitive in the counting categories. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a plug-and-play staple; despite facing the young arm Painter, the combination of his elite profile and a favorable #2 lineup spot makes him a high-floor candidate for multi-category contribution. **Taylor Ward** also warrants attention with a 71.19 score, bolstered by a significant BvP edge (35 PAs) and a favorable hitting environment against Framber Valdez, which optimizes his potential for a productive day in the #1 spot.\n\nStrategic platoon and park factors dictate the remainder of our deployment. **Daulton Varsho** (67.26) is a vital start today, as he gains a 10% efficiency bump from the platoon advantage against Keller, helping us chase those elusive stolen bases. **Luis Arraez** (62.77) and **Matt Chapman** (59.53) both benefit from the wind blowing out, effectively negating the platoon disadvantage against Noah Schultz. On the bench, **Drew Gilbert** (46.46) was the most difficult exclusion; while he possesses strong park-adjusted upside, his #9 spot in the lineup and L/L platoon disadvantage against Schultz ultimately suppressed his score below the threshold required to crack the starting nine. As we await final lineup confirmations for **Will Smith**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Luis Arraez**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Masyn Winn**, **Matt Chapman**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Lawrence Butler**, we must remain alert; any late-breaking lineup shifts could force a pivot from the projected order, though the current depth of our bench\u2014including **Bryson Stott** and **Jonathan Aranda**\u2014ensures we have coverage if weather or rest situations 